Q: Can a Kotlin Object be used as a Spring bean? A: <p>The following should work just fine even though it does not please the eyes</p>
<pre class="lang-kotlin prettyprint-override"><code>interface MyInterface {
    // ...
}

private object MyObject : MyInterface {
    // ...
}

@Configuration
class MyObjectRegistrar {
    @Bean
    @Scope(ConfigurableBeanFactory.SCOPE_SINGLETON)
    fun myObject(): MyInterface = MyObject
}
</code></pre>
